    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 41 Trimbleston is a most attractive, second floor apartment located in front of the development in the Sycamore block. Trimbleston is a prestigious, Sorahan-built development off the Goatstown Road, considered a most desirable location in south Dublin. This modern development comprises a lovely blend of apartments and houses set amidst landscaped gardens. This owner-occupied unit has been well maintained throughout and features accommodation extending to 78sq.m (excluding the balcony); it comprises an entrance hall with a storage closet and hot press, a kitchen that is open plan with the living/dining room, two bedrooms (one en-suite), and a family bathroom. This superb apartment has a generous balcony overlooking private landscaped gardens and is accessible from the living/dining room and master bedroom.\r\n\r\nTrimbleston enjoys a central location; it is within close proximity to Clonskeagh, Milltown, Ranelagh, Dundrum, and Stillorgan, offering an excellent range of shopping centres, speciality shops, restaurants, eateries, schools and sporting amenities. It is within walking distance of UCD. Access to the M50/N11 motorways are close by and the No. 11 bus goes to the City Centre.\r\n\r\nThere are communal gardens with green areas, planted beds and cobble lock pathways throughout the development, and there is a fountain in the main garden. There are paved off street parking spaces for visitors and underground parking"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "HALL\r\nWith ceiling coving, recessed lights and timber floor. There is access to the storage closet and the hot press.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN\r\n5.14m x 2.61m\r\nOpen plan to living/dining area with coved ceiling and recessed lighting with an array of floor and wall mounted Shaker style units with granite worktops, an integrated fridge/freezer and dishwasher. There is a built-in oven with gas hob with overhead extractor fan and it is plumbed for a washing machine.\r\n\r\nLIVING/DINING ROOM\r\n6.22m x 3.71m\r\nThis is a very spacious, well-proportioned and bright room – perfect for entertaining with ample room to dine and it has a large picture window overlooking the gardens and has access to the balcony. It features ceiling coving, recessed and wall lighting and timber flooring and attractive fireplace with electric effect fire provides a focal point for this lovely room.\r\n\r\n\r\nMASTER BEDROOM\r\n3.45m x 3.45m\r\nA large double bedroom overlooking the private gardens, it features ample built in wardrobes and an en-suite. There is access to the balcony.\r\n\r\nEN-SUITE\r\nWith tiled floor and partially tiled walls, w.c., w.h.b. mirrored vanity cabinet, chrome towel rail, and a walk in tiled shower cubicle\r\n\r\nBEDROOM TWO\r\n2.96m x 2.77m\r\nA double bedroom with fitted wardrobe\r\n\r\nBATHROOM\r\n2.17m x 1.82m\r\nWith tiled floor and partially tiled walls, a bath with tiled surround and telephone shower, w.c., w.h.b. and a mirrored vanity cabinet.\r\n\r\nBALCONY\r\n5.05m x 1.70m\r\nThe balcony is accessible from the living room and master bedroom. It is sheltered and not overlooked; it features paved flooring and a glass panelled barrier. \r\n\r\nManagement Company: Indigo Real Estate Management \r\nService Charge: currently €2,971.25 per annum (subject to review)."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Hardwood double glazed windows\r\nHardwood doors and timber flooring\r\n78sq.m approximately\r\nLarge sheltered balcony\r\nCommunal interior and exterior areas meticulously maintained\r\nUnderground parking space and visitor parking\r\nOnsite caretaker"
      },
